If you folks are using `swr` or `react-query`, you don't need to use `useEffect`.
Juste use conditional fetching documented [here](https://swr.vercel.app/docs/conditional-fetching).

```
const router = useRouter()
const { id } = router.query

const { data } = useSWR(id  && `/api/resources/${id}`, fetcher)
```

Because `id` is falsy (can be `null`, `undefined`, `0` or empty), the request won't be performed.
When `id` becomes available, `swr` will perform the request.


You can also use @sirLisko's [suggestion](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/10521#issuecomment-760926715) and use [Router.isReady](https://nextjs.org/docs/api-reference/next/router#router-object):

```
const router = useRouter()
const { id } = router.query

const { data } = useSWR(router.isReady && `/api/resources/${id}`, fetcher)

// Or 
const { data } = useSWR(router.isReady ? `/api/resources/${id}` : null, fetcher)

```

