It seems that this proposal may be too narrowly focused, where it aims to cover client-side navigations for dynamic permission-based pages (where SSR previewing isn't needed). It would simplify some of the boilerplate logic for when a page needs to be conditionally rendered.

For example, a user visits a private page that just requires basic level permissions...

**authSagas.js** (the API request)
```js
/**
 * Client-side attempt to sign into a previous cookie session on initial app load
 *
 * @generator
 * @function signinOnLoad
 * @yields {object} - A response from a call to API.
 * @throws {action} - A redux action to display a server error message.
 * @yields {action} - A redux action to update redux authentication state.
 */
function* signinOnLoad() {
  let data = {};
  try {
    const res = yield call(axios.get, "u/signedin");
    data = res.data
  } catch (e) {
    yield call(setServerError, e.toString());
  } finally {
    yield put(actions.signin(data));
  }
}
```

**_app.js** (initiate API request)
```js
const App = ({ Component, pageProps }) => {
  const role = useSelector(({ authentication }) => authentication.role);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!role) dispatch(signinOnLoad());
  }, []);

  return (
   <>
     <PageContainer>
       <Component {...pageProps} />
     </PageContainer>
     <ServerMessages />
   </>
  );
};

App.propTypes = {
  Component: PropTypes.any,
  pageProps: PropTypes.any,
  role: PropTypes.string
};

export default wrapper.withRedux(App);
```

Then this HOC wraps the authenticated page and would wait for the response...

**withAuthentication.js** (wait for API response)
```js
const withAuthentication = WrappedComponent => {
  const RequiresAuthentication = props => {
    const { email, role } = useSelector(
      ({ authentication, messages }) => ({
        email: authentication.email,
        role: authentication.role,
      })
    );

    // when any users visit this private page they'll be greeted with a Spinner
    // if they're an authenticated user, then they'll be allowed to view the page
    // if they're determined to be a guest, then they'll be redirected to the sign in page
    return role === "guest" ? (
      <Redirect href="/signin"  />
    ) : email ? (
      <WrappedComponent {...props} />
    ) : (
      <Spinner />
    );
  };

  return RequiresAuthentication;
};

withAuthentication.propTypes = {
  WrappedComponent: PropTypes.node.isRequired
};

export default withAuthentication;
